  "decontamination_notes": "Real fix from more-itertools PR #1211, merged 2026-07-13, after model training cutoffs, so the specific fix is novel. Repo sliced at the PR's base commit cb75bb9 (more_itertools package + MIT LICENSE); dependency-free flat-layout package runs on the base sandbox image with PYTHONPATH=.. The bug is in the bounded sliding-window helpers (_windowed_running_min/_windowed_running_max), which used `not a < value` (drops equal values, keeping the newest) instead of `value < a` (keeps the oldest, matching builtin min/max stability). Hidden tests assert observable output of the public running_min/running_max recipes -- yielded values and, on ties, which equal value survives (via type()) -- never the helpers' internal deque state.",
